      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A five-year-old male Bouvier des Flandres was presented with chronic otalgia of approximately four and a half years' duration. Atresia of the external acoustic meatus was diagnosed. A total ear canal ablation and bulla osteotomy were performed. All symptoms of otalgia resolved within two weeks of surgery."},
